}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-5}{2-{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x>0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}-5}{2-{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(1-\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{0-1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106705/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106705"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-302240/field-1/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" :answer/id #uuid "d66a3589-0da5-5f32-ba48-a506c649a6ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302240/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "347827f2-cb32-5655-9539-044dcf23f8a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302240/field-1/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" :answer-field/choices ["q-302240/field-1/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302240" :question/id #uuid "143183aa-b87e-56d7-a491-9ddede7028da" :question/math-academy-id "q-302240" :question/problem "What is the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ for $x<0$ with $f(x)=\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}?$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote is $y=$\n\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "For large negative values of $x,$ we have $|8x-7|=-(8x-7).$ Consequently, for $x\\to -\\infty ,$ we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{|8x-7|}{-5x+2}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2}.\n$$\n\nThe horizontal asymptote for $x<0$ is $y={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8x-7)}{-5x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(\\frac{8x}{x}-\\frac{7}{x})}{(\\frac{-5x}{x}+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{-(8-\\frac{7}{x})}{(-5+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(8-0)}{-5+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{8}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-302240/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee15db10-b92c-5f48-8983-e602068c7e08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302240"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
